    narr:narration """Dave Quantum's voice on 2026-08-15 is a single settled announcement: a database migration from PostgreSQL to QuantumDB, delivered as declarative decision rather than proposal. He opens with the decision itself — [switching to QuantumDB for analytics](narr:Expr_1E2EQuantum1786785433921_1) — then supplies the [rationale in performance and cost terms](narr:Expr_1E2EQuantum1786785433921_2), before restating both as [parallel summary bullets](narr:Expr_1E2EQuantum1786785433921_3) covering [migration](narr:Expr_1E2EQuantum1786785433921_3), [performance gain](narr:Expr_1E2EQuantum1786785433921_4), and [timeline](narr:Expr_1E2EQuantum1786785433921_5). His register is technical throughout, conviction running as decision — the saying enacts the move — with the rationale shifting to claim-level rational persuasion. Style compresses from metaphor in the opening to short-punchy-cadence in the rationale to parallelism across the bullets, an arc from announcement to reference card. The power footing moves with it: informational authority when declaring, reward and rational persuasion when selling benefits, pressure when setting the Q3 deadline.""" ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1E2EQuantum1786785433921_1> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1E2EQuantum1786785433921_2> ;
